# Deployment

**Do not use CDK** for deployments. Use only the specific deploy scripts in the `scripts/` folder.

## Scripts to Use

| Component | Script |
|-----------|--------|
| Backend (Lambda) | `./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh` (updates **API handler** and, when `backend/lambda/loyalty-consumer.zip` exists after build, **warmpawz-dev-loyalty-events-consumer**) |
| Admin Web | `./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh` |
| Vendor Web | `./scripts/deploy-vendor-web.sh` |
| Customer Web | `./scripts/deploy-customer-web.sh` |

## Examples

```bash
# Deploy backend only (dev — default function warmpawz-dev-api-handler)
./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh

# Deploy admin web only (dev)
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh

# Deploy both backend and admin web (dev)
./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh && ./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh
```

## Production (ship backend + admin)

Use the same scripts; prod is selected by **environment variable** (Lambda) and **`--prod`** (admin). Admin injects **prod HTTP API**: `https://mss9sa4y01.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com` (see `scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh`).

```bash
# 1) Backend → prod Lambda (ap-south-1)
LAMBDA_FUNCTION_NAME=warmpawz-prod-api-handler ./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh

# 2) Admin web → prod S3 + CloudFront, runtime config → prod API Gateway
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh --prod

# Non-interactive (e.g. CI): skip the "type yes" prompt
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh --prod --yes

# Both in one line
LAMBDA_FUNCTION_NAME=warmpawz-prod-api-handler ./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh && ./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh --prod
```

Alternate admin URL after deploy: `https://admin.warmpawz.com` (same CloudFront origin as `https://dbr09zyoq9akb.cloudfront.net`; see `prodscripts/PRODUCTION_CONFIG.md`).
